# dev-notes.29 — worker-layout-option-c-test-contract-cleanup-v1

Date: 2026-06-07
Branch/slice: worker-layout-option-c-test-contract-cleanup-v1

## Purpose

Harden `tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs` real-runtime prompt assertions so the test validates the runtime reset/re-init contract without relying on open-ended soft prompt behavior.

## Scope

Modified:

```text
tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
```

Added:

```text
docs/dev-notes.29
```

## Implementation summary

The real-runtime modes in `smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs` now use sentinel-shaped prompts:

```text
RESET_READY
BEFORE_RESET_READY
AFTER_RESET_READY
```

The test adds local helpers for sentinel prompt construction and real-runtime settlement checking. The default assertion now requires the real-runtime prompt to settle with a string result, then warns if the local model returns an empty string or omits the requested sentinel. This keeps the gate focused on the runtime reset/re-init completion and terminal settlement contract instead of failing on small-model output quality or semantic noncompliance.

Set `STRICT_REAL_OUTPUT=1` to make empty real-model output fail. Set `STRICT_REAL_SENTINEL=1` to make missing sentinel text fail when intentionally testing model instruction compliance.

## Preserved behavior

This branch does not change production runtime code. It preserves the same runtime operation ordering in the smoke test:

```text
initModel() -> resetModel() -> prompt() -> shutdownRuntime()
initModel() -> prompt() -> resetModel() -> prompt() -> shutdownRuntime()
initModel(configOverride) -> resetModel() -> prompt() -> shutdownRuntime()
```

Mock-mode deterministic checks and fixture behavior remain unchanged.

## Non-goals

No production runtime behavior, worker routing, lifecycle behavior, config/configOverride behavior, scheduler behavior, stream shaping, fixture architecture, cleanup outside the target test, or optimization changes are included.

## Validation notes

Recommended validation:

```bash
find . -name '*.mjs' -print0 | sort -z | xargs -0 -n1 node --check
node ./tests/tools/checkRuntimeFixtureCoverage.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerProtocolContract.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestLifecycleRegression.mjs
```

Real-runtime validation remains Michael-side because the cleanup targets real-model prompt brittleness. A first strict-sentinel candidate failed on Michael's real runtime because the model produced non-empty text that did not include the requested sentinel after init/reset; v2 recorded that as a model semantic mismatch. A second Michael-side run against v2 produced an empty string after init/reset even though initModel(), resetModel(), and prompt terminal settlement completed. v3 therefore treats both empty real-model output and missing sentinel text as warnings by default, while preserving strict opt-in modes for output-quality or instruction-compliance investigation.
